Package: @PACKAGE_ID@
Name: uutils coreutils
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCHITECTURE@
Description: GNU coreutils rewritten in Rust, for jailbroken iOS
 The uutils reimplementation of the GNU core utilities -- ls, cp, mv, cat,
 sort, dd, du and about a hundred more -- cross-compiled for iOS and packaged
 for both roothide and rootless bootstraps from one arm64 build. The
 architecture field says which layout this package is, not which CPU it runs
 on. Upstream is @UPSTREAM@.
 .
 This takes over the GNU coreutils in usr/bin: one multi-call binary with a
 symlink per utility beside it, unpacked over the files the GNU package owns.
 .
 It conflicts with coreutils deliberately, so no package manager installs it
 by accident -- resolving from a repository would mean removing a package that
 apt, dpkg and Sileo themselves depend on, and they will refuse. Installing it
 is an explicit act:
 .
 `sudo dpkg -i --force-conflicts wiki.qaq.uutils_*.deb`
 .
 That unpacks over the GNU files and leaves the GNU package registered, so
 nothing is deleted and `rm` never leaves PATH. Do NOT feed the .deb to
 `apt install` directly: apt treats a local file as an explicit request and
 will remove coreutils first, which takes `rm` away mid-transaction and wedges
 dpkg with no way back except SSH and the stash this package leaves in
 usr/libexec/uutils/gnu-backup.
 .
 Every process these utilities start goes through posix_spawn(); there is no
 fork() in the binary, no setuid/setgid, and nothing escalates privilege:
 children inherit what the shell had.
 .
 Not included, because they cannot work here: stdbuf (its helper library would
 have to be injected into a platform-signed process), chroot (needs root and
 the credential syscalls this binary denies), chcon and runcon (SELinux).
 getent is not a uutils utility; a small stand-in ships in its place.
Maintainer: OwnGoal Studio <not-gonna-reply@owngoal.dev>
Author: uutils developers <https://github.com/uutils/coreutils>
Section: Utilities
Priority: standard
Depends: firmware (>= @MIN_IOS@)
Provides: md5sum, sha1sum, dirname, kill, mktemp
Replaces: coreutils, system-cmds, shell-cmds (<< 207.40.1), text-cmds (<< 1:0), file-cmds (<< 272.250.1-1)
Conflicts: coreutils, shell-cmds (<< 207.40.1), text-cmds (<< 1:0), file-cmds (<< 272.250.1-1), system-cmds (<< 854.40.2-3)
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
